cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Penthera in research or a report, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Penthera: an offline security scanner for web apps and AI-built code"
abstract: >-
  Penthera is an offline, non-destructive security scanner and Agent Skill. It
  runs black-box checks against a live URL and white-box checks against a
  repository, labels every finding with a confidence level and its provenance,
  maps findings to the OWASP Web Security Testing Guide, and exports SARIF and
  NIS2 evidence. Its methodology and accuracy benchmark are documented in
  docs/METHODOLOGY.md and bench/RESULTS.md.
authors:
  - family-names: "van der Zwaag"
    given-names: "Daan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/danoszz/penthera"
url: "https://github.com/danoszz/penthera"
license: MIT
version: 2.1.2
date-released: 2026-10-22
keywords:
  - security
  - vulnerability scanner
  - black-box testing
  - static analysis
  - secret detection
  - SARIF
  - OWASP
  - NIS2
